# Who may ask the Astra registry to list a plugin out of this repository.
#
# The registry reads this file over GitHub's public contents API, on the
# default branch, at the moment it checks — so being able to write it here is
# the proof. It says nothing about the code, and it is not a signature.
#
# Removing a login stops that account opening a new listing request or passing
# a `/recheck`. It does not reach a plugin that is already listed: every
# release after the first is proved against the account that published it.
#
# One login per line. See docs/en/5-publish/get-listed.md § "Prove you control
# the repository".
